oof\n\n**Item 1** (`tools/pr/prepr.sh` step 3f3). The step ran the tool into `/tmp/prepr-fc.$$`, summarized it with `tail -1` only, and removed the file on the next line — so when the run refused, the `BLIND`/`DEAD`/`REFUSED` cause lines sat in a file nobody could read after the step returned (#2118). Mutant = the old expression, driven against a real refusing run (registry arm, refusal engineered by a temporary bogus `DECLARED` key, restored after):\n\n- old expression, rc=1: `detail=[FIELD COVERAGE REFUSED: a BLIND field, a DEAD entry or a REFUSED run above]` — and the file carrying `DEAD     registry: DECLARED \\`no-such-check-engineered-2134\\` is no longer in the derived set` is then `rm -f`'d.\n- fixed expression, same refusal: `detail=[ DEAD registry: DECLARED \\`no-such-check-engineered-2134\\` is no longer in the derived set;FIELD COVERAGE REFUSED: ... ]`\n\nThe fix uses the file's own refusal style — `grep` the cause markers beside `tail -1`, as the `hooks` and `codeowners_gap` steps already do.\n\n**Item 2** (`tools/policy/agreement.mjs` lines 29 and 69; `tools/policy/field_coverage.mjs` lines 39 and 41). Mutant = the retired paths, shown live: `node tools/policy/agreement.mjs` refused with `run \\`python3 -I .claude/workflows/agreement_py.py --run\\``, and `ls .claude/workflows/agreement_py.py` answers `No such file or directory` while `ls tools/policy/agreement_py.py` resolves; `git ls-tree origin/main` shows `agreement.mjs`, `agreement_py.py`, `field_coverage.mjs` only under `tools/policy/`. After: the same refusal prints `run \\`python3 -I tools/policy/agreement_py.py --run\\`` — a path that exists. The `at()`/`locate()` move-map reads at lines 98/99/126/146 and 119/144/206 are untouched: they resolve by design (counts.mjs) and R9-RO-9 owns their spelling.\n\n## Null control\n\n- `bash tools/pr/prepr.sh --self-test` passes 248/248 with the old expression restored — the existing harness does not pin this step's summary, so the engineered-refusal runs above are the evidence, not a check. A self-test arm for it is owed to no rule here and would spend prepr.sh lines for a summary string.\n- `node tools/policy/field_coverage.mjs --only registry` on the unmodified tool is green; the refusal above was engineered and the tool restored byte-identical.\n\n## Figures\n\n- `node tools/policy/policy_lint.mjs --budgets` — the policy rule at 153/153 lines and 1883/1887 tokens, paid by tightening three passages in the same file; no raise.\n- `node tools/policy/rules_sync.mjs --check` — generated copies in sync.\n- `node tools/policy/policy_lint.mjs` — TOTAL: 0 error(s) across 40 policy file(s), fixture pins holding.\n- `python3 tests/structure.py` — STRUCTURE RATCHET PASSED, re-run on a clean checkout carrying only this diff (the shared worktree held another seat's in-flight edits).\n- `bash tools/pr/prepr.sh --self-test` — 248 passed, 0 failed.\n- `node tools/policy/field_coverage.mjs` — FIELD COVERAGE ok, 139 runs.\n- `python3 -I tools/policy/agreement_py.py --out /tmp/ag-2134.json` then `node tools/policy/agreement.mjs --py-json /tmp/ag-2134.json` — AGREEMENT ok.\n\n## Red checks\n\n`delivery-status:failure`, read from the check-runs API (not `gh pr checks`). The check grades `main`'s row-draining at the pinned base (`PINNED=664a4c05e`): one overdue row, #2170 at 13 commits — no merge of this branch is in its table, and the diff touches no input the check reads (its script, `tests.yml`, `governance.yml`, the plan, `HANDOVER.md`, no delivery row), so `defect-root-cause.md`'s Enforcement exemption applies: the red is the orchestrator's on `main`, and the repair is draining #2170's row. The check is not a required context and prints that it blocks no merge. Root-cause answer: no cheaper detector exists — the delivery-status check is the earliest reader of the plan's table, so the gate that caught the stalled batch is the cheapest one.\n\nAll other checks green or in progress at the API read; no cancelled run.\n\n## Forward-carry\n\n`none` — nothing here constrains a later stage; #2134 stays with its disposer.\n\n## Friction\n\n- `tools/policy/agreement.mjs: stale: its own refusal named a run command at a path retired from the tree` (fixed here).\n- `tools/policy/field_coverage.mjs: stale: same retired-path usage comments` (fixed here).\n\n## Approval\n\nThe diff touches policy (`dev/governance/rules/defect-root-cause.md`, and its two generated copies): the `## Approval` gate applies, and the orchestrator posts this review request under mandate 6151222764. The raise question does not arise — the caps command above shows the edit paid for inside the existing file cap.\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T21:43:33Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T22:09:58Z","closed_at":"2026-10-13T22:09:55Z","merged_at":"2026-10-13T22:09:55Z","merge_commit_sha":"a5dfe69bf1d38166f6990b55a7108f5f17a9e9cf","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2178/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2178/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2178/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/statuses/1e4ede5beb3e2c17dcbb69ad3304eb9c5384c2c5","head":{"label":"tvofi:fix/friction-2134","ref":"fix/friction-2134","sha":"1e4ede5beb3e2c17dcbb69ad3304eb9c5384c2c5","user":{"login":"tvofi","id":70032254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMDMyMjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/t